{
  "answer": "It is not possible to delete photos from your phone without also deleting them from iCloud if you are using iCloud Photos Library. The system syncs changes across devices, so deletion on one device removes the iCloud copy. To keep photos in the cloud while freeing phone space, use a third-party service like Dropbox or Amazon Photos, or disable iCloud sync after transferring photos to another storage. Alternatively, you can enable 'Optimize iPhone Storage' in iCloud settings to store lower-resolution files on your phone while keeping full-resolution in iCloud, but this does not delete photos.",
  "citations": ["3", "5", "6", "4"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

{
  "answer": "To delete photos from your phone without deleting them from iCloud, disable iCloud Photo Library on your iPhone. Go to Settings > iCloud > Photos, tap 'iCloud Photo Library', and select 'Remove from iPhone'. This deletes local copies while keeping them in iCloud. Alternatively, you can upload photos to a computer and then delete them from the phone after turning off iCloud Photo Library. Note: With iCloud Photo Library enabled, deletions sync across all devices.",
  "citations": ["5", "6"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

