  "answer": "Yes, PVST+ can interoperate with Rapid Spanning Tree Protocol (RSTP) when properly configured, but it may require careful planning and can be fragile. Specifically, RSTP maps to the PVST+ VLAN 1 instance, and PVST+ BPDUs can be transparently forwarded across an RSTP region if VLAN 1 is trunked. However, mixing rapid STP versions (RSTP and PVST+) can lead to compatibility issues and strange behavior; in some cases, it may be advisable to use slower STP or disable STP on interconnecting links.",
