{
  "answer": "To make an iTunes song your ringtone, first select the song in iTunes, right-click it, choose 'Get Info', go to the 'Options' tab, and set a start and stop time (ringtones must be 40 seconds or less). Then, with the song highlighted, go to File > Convert > Create AAC Version. This creates a duplicate. Right-click the new short version, select 'Show in Finder' (Mac) or 'Show in Windows Explorer' (PC), and rename the file extension from .m4a to .m4r. Confirm the change. Delete the short version from iTunes (keeping the file), then drag the .m4r file back into iTunes (it will appear under Tones). Sync your iPhone with iTunes, enable 'Sync Tones', and select your ringtone. After syncing, go to iPhone Settings > Sounds > Ringtone to set it.",
  "citations": ["lotte_technology_search_100k_c56972", "lotte_technology_search_100k_c1104", "lotte_technology_search_100k_c75285"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

