{
  "answer": "To make an iTunes song your ringtone, you can use iTunes on your computer: first, right-click the song and select 'Get Info', then set start and stop times (ringtone must be under 40 seconds). Click OK, then right-click again and select 'Create AAC Version'. A duplicate will appear. Right-click the duplicate, choose 'Show in Finder' (Mac) or 'Show in Windows Explorer' (PC), and rename the file extension from .m4a to .m4r. Drag the .m4r file back into iTunes (into the Tones section). Sync your iPhone with 'Sync Tones' enabled. Alternatively, on iPhone you can use GarageBand: open GarageBand, create a new song, record or import the song, then tap the share icon and choose 'Ringtone' to export it directly to your ringtones.",
