  "answer": "To make an iTunes song your ringtone, first select the song in iTunes. Right-click it, choose 'Get Info', go to the 'Options' tab, and set a start and stop time (ringtone must be 40 seconds or less). Click OK, then select the song and go to File > Create New Version > Create AAC Version. A shorter duplicate appears. Right-click the duplicate and select 'Show in Finder' (or 'Show in Windows Explorer'). In the Finder window, rename the file's extension from .m4a to .m4r. Confirm the change. Back in iTunes, delete the short version (choose 'Keep File'). Double-click the .m4r file in Finder to add it to your iTunes Tones library. Connect your iPhone to iTunes, click the phone icon, select 'Tones', enable 'Sync Tones', choose the ringtone, and apply. On your iPhone, go to Settings > Sounds & Haptics > Ringtone and select your new tone.",
